{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661964-derped-here-how-to-calculate-damage","id":661964,"title":"Derped here, how to calculate damage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-12T08:41:57-07:00","id":661964,"title":"Derped here, how to calculate damage?","content":"Got mixed up. How dos ya calculares/roll dmg? Did ya added yer strg + The weapon dmg? Or did ya roll dmg diff 6 and EVERY success was dmg?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T12:22:46-07:00","id":662104,"title":"","content":"You got the dice pool calculation for most close combat attacks correct. You then have to roll it and count successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T02:10:22-07:00","id":662828,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember that extra successes (success past the first) each at a die of damage as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T16:14:44-07:00","id":663536,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the damage dice pool is Strength + x + successes beyond the first on the attack roll (difficulty 6).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T04:00:17-07:00","id":673049,"title":"","content":"Damage is a Base value plus the success threshold. You roll it after a hit, the enemy rolls soak if it can, difference applies as damage.<br /> Base damage is usually your STR + Something, like a sword's str+2 or a punch's str+0. Firearms usually have fixed values, like 4, or 3, or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:04:39-08:00","id":771744,"title":"","content":"I love cWoD until Combat Rules. Then I hate it...<br /> <br /> You'll most likely make 4 rolls in combat. As people said, Dex + Hability to hit, dif of the weapon, then the defender will roll Dex + Hability IF she choose to defend. Then you'll take all successes not negated by the defender after 1st, plus Str, plus Weapon Dmg, and roll it on dif 6, no Rule of 1 applied at all, then the defender will roll Stamina or not, depending on the Dmg Type and in her splat, also dif 6 without Rule of 1, then you'll apply the successes on your last roll not negated by her last roll as actual damage.<br /> <br /> And then she will either use a power to Regenerate or igore Pain, or will simply cease to fight, because anything beyond 1 damage will hamper her, anything beyond 3 damage will hamper her A LOT. The first to run out of regen loses, because combat isn't just lethal, it simply sucks...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T03:25:09-08:00","id":772197,"title":"","content":"Sorry to hijack.<br /> <br /> I heard nWoD combat rolls are much more streamlined.<br /> <br /> Anyone have a good nWoD combat rules for oWoD stats translation?<br /> <br /> I'm looking at the Combat Summary Chart in Reap The Whirlwind, and my hunch it to substitute Stamina+Armor+Fortitude for defense, but I can just foresee situations where a vampire with even modest stats just never gets hurt. Additionally, I see no reference to damage types.<br /> <br /> Another combat derp on my part:<br /> Could I get some clarification on how Dodge works? Lets say Char X swings a bat at Char Y, and Char Y dodges. Does Char Y get to do anything on their turn? I suspect not, otherwise there would be no reason not to dodge, but still, I need a ruling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5238,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","user":"Herbert_West","date":". 11-23-2015, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T12:26:05-08:00","id":772454,"title":"","content":"The nWOD has different combat rules for each edition. Translating them to the cWOD isn't hard, but might require some tweaking to get the numbers right. I'm going to stick with nWOD 2e, because it's an easier conversion.<br /> <br /> The only big change would to have Wits replace Composure for the calculations. So you would have a defense equal to the lower of Dexterity or Wits, + Athletics (for avoiding attacks)/Brawl (blocks)/Melee (parry). This would be a flat value reflexively subtracted from attacks against you, but -1 for each such attack. You can raise it by +2 against one attack by spending a WP.<br /> <br /> If you spend the whole turn defending, you double your defense value and roll it against attacks (the -1 each time turns into -2 dice), and can still spend a WP on one roll to boost it.<br /> <br /> Damage is Strength (if applies) + Weapon damage + Extra successes as a flat value, and you subtract Stamina (if the target can soak the damage) + Armor from it. Unless magical armors that say so apply, a hit target always takes a minimum of 1 bashing if the attack would have been reduced to zero.<br /> <br /> The weapon damage vs. armor values would need adjusting, A shotgun with 8 damage would be an automatic kill on a normal human that isn't wearing armor with even one success. Probably... divide the cWOD weapon damages by half.<br /> <br /> Anything that would normally boost the relevant Attributes/Abilities would also probably need some tweaking. Specialties normally double 10s, so that's useless for unrolled stuff. Anything that provides a diff modifier to defense would likewise need adjusting.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> In RAW cWOD, defense rolls can be split. You can dodge and attack, but at penalties to both (how much/etc. depends on edition). If you apply your full dodge roll against an attack, that's your action for the turn (unless you're using one of the cWOD rule sets that allow for &quot;full defense&quot; which allows you to get multiple dodges in a turn, but you can still only defend).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T02:45:24-08:00","id":775342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661964-derped-here-how-to-calculate-damage?p=772454#post772454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nWOD has different combat rules for each edition. Translating them to the cWOD isn't hard, but might require some tweaking to get the numbers right. I'm going to stick with nWOD 2e, because it's an easier conversion.<br /> <br /> The only big change would to have Wits replace Composure for the calculations. So you would have a defense equal to the lower of Dexterity or Wits, + Athletics (for avoiding attacks)/Brawl (blocks)/Melee (parry). This would be a flat value reflexively subtracted from attacks against you, but -1 for each such attack. You can raise it by +2 against one attack by spending a WP.<br /> <br /> If you spend the whole turn defending, you double your defense value and roll it against attacks (the -1 each time turns into -2 dice), and can still spend a WP on one roll to boost it.<br /> <br /> Damage is Strength (if applies) + Weapon damage + Extra successes as a flat value, and you subtract Stamina (if the target can soak the damage) + Armor from it. Unless magical armors that say so apply, a hit target always takes a minimum of 1 bashing if the attack would have been reduced to zero.<br /> <br /> The weapon damage vs. armor values would need adjusting, A shotgun with 8 damage would be an automatic kill on a normal human that isn't wearing armor with even one success. Probably... divide the cWOD weapon damages by half.<br /> <br /> Anything that would normally boost the relevant Attributes/Abilities would also probably need some tweaking. Specialties normally double 10s, so that's useless for unrolled stuff. Anything that provides a diff modifier to defense would likewise need adjusting.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> In RAW cWOD, defense rolls can be split. You can dodge and attack, but at penalties to both (how much/etc. depends on edition). If you apply your full dodge roll against an attack, that's your action for the turn (unless you're using one of the cWOD rule sets that allow for &quot;full defense&quot; which allows you to get multiple dodges in a turn, but you can still only defend).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Many thanks. How do you deal with the &quot;to hit&quot; Dice Pool potentially being reduced to zero just by stats? One can easily see situations where a characters defense stat is so high that they can just not get hit. Do you enforce a &quot;pool is never less than 1&quot; rule? Otherwise, I can easily see players getting really frustrated,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T07:31:35-08:00","id":775452,"title":"","content":"Well, the nWOD has a &quot;if reduced to zero, you can roll a chance die,&quot; for that. It's easy enough to port to the cWOD, it's 1d10 diff 10.<br /> <br /> The difference is that in the nWOD, spending a WP on a roll nets you +3 dice (statistically average of 1 success in that system), instead of a raw success. Something else you can do is let someone spend a WP for 1 auto success even if reduced to zero dice.<br /> <br /> Another thing to import is probably the &quot;all out attack&quot; maneuver from the nWOD where you sacrifice your passive Defense for extra attack dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T15:27:07-08:00","id":776838,"title":"","content":"So just so I understand, and so that there is a paper trail:<br /> <br /> Lets have two characters. Character A attacks Character B, so initiative is out. Both characters have melee weapons, and character B wears Armour.<br /> <br /> Character A has Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Melee 2, and is wielding a weapon with a damage rating of 4.<br /> Character B has a Dexterity of 2, a Wits of 3, and an Athletics score of 1, and a Melee of 5, and a Stamina of 2. He has a weapon of damage rating 1, and a armor of rating 1.<br /> <br /> <i>The &quot;to hit roll&quot; is thus:</i><br /> Char A: Dex (3) + Char A: Melee (2) - Char B: Dexterity (2) - Char B: Athletics (1), for a total <i>dice pool </i>of 2.<br /> <br /> The dice come up as 6 and 7, a hit, and one carryover damage.<br /> <br /> Damage dealt: Is this a dice pool, or a flat number?<br /> Char A:Weapon damage stat (Strength, 3) + Char A:Weapon damage bonus (2) + To hit roll: Extra successes (1) - Char B:Stamina (2) - Char B:Armor (1), for a total <i>dice pool</i> of 3<br /> <br /> Correct so far?<br /> <br /> <br /> Problems arise when the Defender opts to Parry. In our case, the dice pool for character B parrying is higher than the dice pool of Character A for attacking. How do you handle this? Do you fall back on the &quot;both roll, whoever wins gets to deal damage&quot; rule, as per RAW of VTM20? Otherwise, there is no reason not to parry, ever.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if Char B opts to do nothing but defend, how does that work? Do we now have to go back to rolling the to hit for char A (Dex+Melee), a dice pool of five against the doubled defense dice pool of Char B, which is six, as if it were a resisted roll in RAW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T19:22:59-08:00","id":776944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/661964-derped-here-how-to-calculate-damage?p=776838#post776838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damage dealt: Is this a dice pool, or a flat number?<br /> Char A:Weapon damage stat (Strength, 3) + Char A:Weapon damage bonus (2) + To hit roll: Extra successes (1) - Char B:Stamina (2) - Char B:Armor (1), for a total <i>dice pool</i> of 3<br /> <br /> Correct so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're trying to be more like that nWOD it would be 3 damage, not dice. Hence cutting back on the cWOD damage tags is pretty important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Problems arise when the Defender opts to Parry. In our case, the dice pool for character B parrying is higher than the dice pool of Character A for attacking. How do you handle this? Do you fall back on the &quot;both roll, whoever wins gets to deal damage&quot; rule, as per RAW of VTM20? Otherwise, there is no reason not to parry, ever. </div> </div> </div>The rolled version in the nWOD is the equivalent to the &quot;full defense&quot; option in some cWOD games. Parrying shouldn't do damage in this case. A counterstriking parry should be its own combat maneuver that counts as your action, and is a basic roll off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, if Char B opts to do nothing but defend, how does that work? Do we now have to go back to rolling the to hit for char A (Dex+Melee), a dice pool of five against the doubled defense dice pool of Char B, which is six, as if it were a resisted roll in RAW? </div> </div> </div>Yes, but keep in mind that B's dice pool is reduced by two for every attack they have to deal with, and it's a split action. So A (I know there's some variations that don't quite work this way) could split a &quot;feint&quot; attack with one die, and a follow up for 4 dice, while B has to roll 6 dice against the first, and four for the second.<br /> <br /> This can slow things down, but keeping in mind that without magic, any successful hit does some damage, once wound penalties start coming into play for a character trying to go full defense, it will eventually fail them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T02:36:17-08:00","id":777067,"title":"","content":"Much obliged. <br /> <br /> Yeah, damage probably needs to be dampened hard. One of my PCs mouthed off to a couple of Brujah Antitribu, and promptly got herself pummeled into unconsciousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}